WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.868
-The world was
heartbroken yesterday

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.737
by a helicopter accident
in Los Angeles

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:06.706
that claimed the lives
of nine people,

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.474
including that of Kobe Bryant

00:00:08.474 --> 00:00:11.110
and his 13-year-old
daughter Gianna.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.613
Kobe was such a life force,
so strong and creative

00:00:14.613 --> 00:00:16.315
and inspired
that in my head,

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:18.585
I thought that he was going
to live forever.

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:22.021
I met Kobe when he was 17
and I was 21.

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:23.522
He was a rookie on the Lakers,

00:00:23.522 --> 00:00:25.991
and I was just starting out
in the comedy scene in L.A.

00:00:25.991 --> 00:00:27.827
We were at a party, and we
didn't know anyone the party,

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:29.195
so we just started talking.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.763
And I said, like,
"Hey, what do you do?"

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:32.265
And he goes,
"I play basketball."

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:36.002
I go, "Where?"
And he goes, "For the Lakers."

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.804
I go, "Wow."
He goes, "What do you do?"

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:39.572
I go, "I'm a stand-up comic."
We just got along,

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.107
we hit it off, started talking.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.476
He was telling me he was into
poetry, and I met his sister.

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:45.110
She was there.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:48.214
And so, then, the guy that was
having the party said,

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.717
"Hey, guys, who wants to make
a beer run?"

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.685
And Kobe wasn't drinking.
He was 17.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:53.953
So he goes, "I'll do it."

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.287
He goes,
"Jimmy, you want to come?"

00:00:55.287 --> 00:00:57.356
So I go, "Okay."
So, I get in the car,

00:00:57.356 --> 00:00:58.624
it was me and Kobe Bryant.

00:00:58.624 --> 00:01:00.526
And we -- he's brand-new
in L.A., and me too.

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:01.861
I didn't know L.A. at all.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.263
And we drive down
Sunset Boulevard

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:05.598
to this place called
Pink Dot.

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.166
It looked like a 7-Eleven.

00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:08.668
Well, I thought it was
a 7-Eleven.

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.836
You pulled in. And --
But it wasn't a 7-Eleven.

00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:14.206
Anyway, so I go in, and I
open the door and it's locked.

00:01:14.206 --> 00:01:17.377
And the guy goes, "Sorry,
I can't sell you anything."

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:20.380
And I go, "We just want to get
some beer right there."

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.047
And he goes,
"Yeah, I can't do that."

00:01:22.047 --> 00:01:23.683
And I go, "But just real quick,
we know what it is.

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:25.185
It's just there."
And he goes,

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:27.353
"Yeah, that's not how --
the way this place works.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:30.389
We're delivery only. We're not
allowed to sell things."

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:32.458
And I go, "Uh, okay."

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:34.060
And then Kobe
takes out his I.D.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.095
and he puts it up against
the glass and he goes,

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:38.831
"I'm a Laker."
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:41.567
And the guy opened the door,
and we walked out

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:44.570
with five cases of beer
and we saved the party.

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:46.639
So we saved the party,
we say good night,

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:49.175
and of course Kobe
went on to become a legend.

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:52.378
Five NBA titles,
two Olympic gold medals,

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.414
18 All-Star appearances.

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.348
One of the most brilliant
and most respected players

00:01:56.348 --> 00:01:58.150
in NBA history.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:01:59.818
And when we'd run into each
other over the years,

00:01:59.818 --> 00:02:01.720
we'd laugh about that night
that we first met.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.990
[ Crying ]

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.759
[ Clears throat ]

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:10.896
We'd laugh at all the good
things that had happened since.

00:02:10.896 --> 00:02:13.066
And we'd laugh at how much fun
it was to raise kids

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.867
and all the stupid mistakes
we made

00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:18.504
trying to figure out
how to be good dads.

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:22.575
And Kobe had four daughters,
and I had two daughters.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:26.178
And today, he and one of
his girls are gone.

00:02:26.178 --> 00:02:28.447
But I think I knew Kobe enough
to know that he rose

00:02:28.447 --> 00:02:31.885
to any challenge by digging
deeper and getting back to work.

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:33.352
So let's honor Kobe, Gianna,

00:02:33.352 --> 00:02:35.020
and the other lives
that were lost yesterday

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.856
by following his example.

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:39.358
Love your family,
love your teammates,

00:02:39.358 --> 00:02:42.462
and outwork everyone
else in the gym.

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.830
To Vanessa and all those
affected by this tragedy,

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:47.232
we love you and will always be
there for all of you.

00:02:47.232 --> 00:02:49.802
Kobe, when we meet again,

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.771
we're going on a beer run.

